# Commercial S11.2 R15.3 systemd repository access

## Classification

`CONTROLLER_SUPPLEMENTARY_GROUP_MISSING`

The R15.2 natural controller run executed as `User=root` and `Group=root` with
only the primary `root` group. The capability boundary intentionally excluded
`CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE`. Repository parents remained `chatops:chatops:2770`, so the
controller could not traverse to the application virtual-environment Python
entrypoint and exited with status 126.

## Minimal contract correction

The canonical unit adds exactly `SupplementaryGroups=chatops`. `User`, `Group`,
capabilities, sandboxing, read/write paths, repository ownership and repository
modes remain unchanged. No sudoers, SSH, Tailscale, ACL or firewall setting is
modified.

The source fixture proves the old effective group set returns the shell-equivalent
exit status 126 for a protected repository parent, while the corrected group set
permits traversal. Deployment must additionally execute a product-read-only
access preflight in the same systemd sandbox before `START_CANARY`.

## Runtime safety contract

The deploy lock is released only after all Canary-OFF gates, synthetic journeys,
fallback checks and the bounded epoch transition are complete. The timer is then
enabled and the deployment waits for a distinct timer-driven controller
invocation. A non-zero result, repeated exit 126 or timeout triggers the existing
versioned rollback and forbids a second Canary attempt.

Real acquisition and its `2026-09-18T00:41:06.710027Z` baseline are preserved.
Human acceptance remains deferred. Adult media, real AVS, payments, external
publishing, Controlled Beta and production remain closed.
